WEBVTT

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.996
Rosa is a tool and system for handling
passwords, which makes it easy to be more

00:00:07.996 --> 00:00:08.800
secure online.

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.120
Here's how it works.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.580
The password you enter into websites when
you log in is made up of two halves.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.480
Half your password is something you always
use.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.580
The other half is something unique just for
that site.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.500
You can trust Rosa with the unique half of
your password.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.580
Let's say you're trying to set a password
for Amazon.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:33.080
919Zap# is your half, which you have
memorized and never share with Rosa.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:37.560
This is the half of your password, which
will be the same on all websites you use.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:40.820
brightidea is the other half, which is
unique for Amazon.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.620
You give Rosa that half of the password,
like this.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:49.338
I'll store my password for Amazon by sending
a text message to Rosa, telling her I

00:00:49.338 --> 00:00:51.040
want to store a password for Amazon.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:01.452
I'm only telling Rosa half the password, the
unique part for each website, which is

00:01:01.452 --> 00:01:02.780
brightidea in this case.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:06.980
I'll never tell Rosa my half, the 919Zap#.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:12.020
Also, notice I never set up a user account
or gave Rosa my username or any other

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:13.180
personal information.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.120
She just knows my phone number because I'm
texting her.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:20.620
Later I want to log into Amazon and need to
know the full password.

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:22.500
I ask Rosa for her half.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:38.860
And to log into Amazon, I combine my half
919Zap# with what Rosa just told me.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:39.820
brightidea.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.520
And if you have a Mac and an iPhone, it's
even easier.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:51.360
You can use iMessage on your Mac to type
your messages to Rosa using your keyboard.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.840
Then when Rosa's half of the password is
texted back to me,

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:58.060
I can open it right on my computer and copy
it to the clipboard.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.160
Have fun being more secure with Rosa.
